cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "vcibayes: layered Bayesian networks for cohort studies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Overmars
    given-names: Malin
    name-suffix: PhD
    affiliation: "UMC Utrecht, Vascular Cognitive Impairment research group"
repository-code: "https://github.com/umcu/vci-bayes"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.17305046
    description: "Concept DOI for all versions"
abstract: >-
  vcibayes learns knowledge-guided Bayesian networks from cohort data. An
  expert-defined ordering of variable layers constrains structure learning so
  arcs may only run downstream through the layers, and non-random dropout is
  modelled explicitly as a selection layer downstream of the outcomes. The
  analysis is declared in a YAML spec rather than in code: layers and their
  order, network variants, discretisation, seed, bootstrap counts, scenario
  profiles and sensitivity sweeps. Also provides bootstrap edge-stability
  estimates, mutual-information rankings, and single-knob sensitivity analysis
  with an overadjustment check.
keywords:
  - Bayesian network
  - structure learning
  - cohort study
  - vascular cognitive impairment
  - pyAgrum
